Spec: Native owned-runtime authority fixture

Purpose:
  Exercise actual platform-owned frpc processes against the authenticated backend with independent nonexportable client keys.

Owns:
  ./main.go

Structure:
  ./stun.go: Loopback-only bounded two-observation UDP fixture for actual XTCP transport verification.

Must:
  Read only public client CSRs from a protected test directory, generate CA/server private keys in process and publish only public certificates and loopback listener metadata.
  Approve exact fixture device/application/service scopes and use explicit authenticated backend construction without legacy listeners.
  Bound lifetime and permit fixture revocation through an owned marker only; close every owned listener, gate and database on exit.
  Never install, deploy, print credentials or expose fixture administration over the network.
  Optionally enroll a public Android CSR with a separate exact access grant and independent owner marker revocation, preserving Windows fixture scopes.

  Keep the independent Android SDK consumer grant separate from the private-bridge fixture grant, with its own revocation marker.
